  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "driver-module",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/modules/attachments.ts",
      "supports": "getAttachmentsForTest validates the test ID and runs the shared executor's items path for get_attachments_for_test, which the descriptor declares unregistered: it has no page or all helper. Called with no options it sends no limit or offset, and it returns the unwrapped list alone."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-paginated-list",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/modules/paginated-list.ts",
      "supports": "An unregistered operation is still allowed through the executor's items path, which appends limit and offset only when they are defined and returns unwrapList's result."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-list",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/modules/list.ts",
      "supports": "listOf accepts a bare array or an envelope whose collection key is present, and unwrapList returns the collection alone: an envelope's offset, limit, size and _links do not survive it. A null collection is an empty list and any other outer shape throws."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-validation",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/validation.ts",
      "supports": "validateId accepts a positive safe integer; validateEntryId accepts only a UUID, case-insensitively, with nothing before or after it; validatePaginationParams holds limit to 1..250 and offset to a non-negative integer."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-schema",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/schemas/attachments.ts",
      "supports": "AttachmentSchema is one passthrough object for every attachment shape TestRail documents: the upload reply, the legacy case and test entries, the plan, plan-entry and run entries with entity_attachments_id and icon_name, and the 7.1 cloud entries whose id is a UUID string. Every field is nullish and id and entity_id admit a number or a string, so each documented entity parses unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "testrail-attachments",
      "url": "https://support.testrail.com/hc/en-us/articles/7077196481428-Attachments",
      "supports": "get_attachments_for_test/{test_id} requires TestRail 5.7 or later, lists the attachments of a test's results, documents no limit, offset or other filter, and returns the same response format as get_attachments_for_case, whose documented examples are paged envelopes. It answers 400 for an invalid test ID and 403 for no access or insufficient permissions."
    }
  ],
  "input_policy": {
    "ordinary_fields": "reject",
    "custom_fields": "reject",
    "notes": "Strictness is an MCP boundary requirement. The endpoint documents no filters and no paging, so the input is the test ID alone: query and _mcp are refused rather than given controls TestRail does not document."
  },
  "outer_result": {
    "driver": "array",
    "tool_data": "array",
    "notes": "The driver returns the attachments of one reply as a plain array, whether TestRail sent an envelope or a bare array. An envelope's offset, limit, size and _links are dropped by the driver, so a continuation link, if TestRail sends one, is not reported."
  },
